vidence":"Cleveland, Ohio – November 3, 2020 -- Sweeping Corp of America (\"SCA\"), the largest power sweeping company in the United States, today announced that Warburg Pincus, a leading global private equity firm focused on growth investing, has entered into an agreement to acquire the company from the previous investor, Soundcore Capital Partners.","verified":null},{"key":"pr:9d2b1b6208bc329e5cd8ab304061fe20","date":"2020-11-02","date_text":null,"kind":"company_acquisition","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Watford Holdings Ltd.","portco_name":"Watford Holdings Ltd.","target_website":null,"investor":"Arch Capital Group Ltd.","sponsor_is_investor":false,"sponsor_role":"co_investor","co_investors":["Warburg Pincus","Kelso & Company"],"seller":null,"round":null,"stake_pct":30.0,"amount":700000000.0,"currency":"USD","amount_basis":"equity_value","valuation":null,"valuation_currency":null,"headline":"Arch Capital Group Ltd. and Watford Holdings Ltd. Enter into Revised Merger Agreement with an All-Cash Offer of $35.00 per Share, Representing a 12.5% Increase Over Prior Agreement","summary":"Arch agreed to buy Watford at $35.00 per share in cash through a vehicle owned about 40% by Arch and about 30% each by Warburg Pincus and Kelso.","source_name":"Warburg Pincus","source_url":"https://warburgpincus.com/2020/11/02/arch-capital-group-ltd-and-watford-holdings-ltd-enter-into-revised-merger-agreement-with-an-all-cash-offer-of-35-00-per-share-representing-a-12-5-increase-over-prior-agreement/","evidence":"This revised all-cash consideration is valued at approximately $700 million and represents a premium of approximately 96% to Watford’s unaffected closing common share price on September 8, 2020, the last trading day prior to media reports about the possibility of a transaction between Watford and Arch.","verified":true},{"key":"pr:eb3fca8f027daae199a819de8e439729","date":"2020-11-02","date_text":null,"kind":"company_exit","asset_class":"private_equity","target":"Ser